    "done_when": "Done when a log under the run directory records, beside the §1 figures, the median of every read it ran, cold and warm, for roadmap, audit and discovery. Those include at least the reads the deliverable's completion floor names, and any read the hour cut is named as not run. Three medians carry targets and are marked against them: a warm median of at most 2 s for roadmap and 3 s for audit, and a cold roadmap under the 30 s MCP deadline. Cold audit and both discovery medians carry no target and are recorded beside the §1 figures for comparison only. This measurement decides whether the fixes from §8 to §17 meet the targets. Every target this run misses is attributed from the kept profile dumps: functions covering at least 80 percent of the excess are named, with the commits that introduced them, and the repair is proposed as a new section of this plan, as the 2026-10-16 measurement proposed §16 and §17. A missed target attributed that way completes this node. Once every target is met, roadmap(project=\"reckon\") through the MCP server, restarted on the promoted code, returns without storage-slow . The negative control is the base revision measured the same way in the same session, which must exceed the deadline for the comparison to count. Both arms run on an exclusive all_debug node in the same window. Each log names the code revision it measured, the pinned corpus revision, the host it ran on and its literal command. Every profiler .prof dump and the pinned corpus revision are copied into the run directory before the job ends, as §7 keeps its dumps, so a missed target is attributed from them rather than from node-local scratch. Write paths: the run directory.",
